{"causes": ["Infanta Philippa's birth into the Portuguese House of Aviz, as the daughter of Infante Peter, Duke of Coimbra, provided her with royal status and dynastic importance.", "The ongoing political rivalries and need for strategic alliances among the powerful noble families of 15th-century Portugal necessitated dynastic marriages.", "The significant wealth and influence of the House of Braganza made a matrimonial alliance highly desirable for strengthening ties within the Portuguese aristocracy."], "effects": ["Her marriage to Don Álvaro de Braganza significantly strengthened the dynastic ties between the House of Aviz (through the Coimbra branch) and the powerful House of Braganza.", "She became an ancestress of the future Dukes of Braganza, whose lineage would eventually ascend to the Portuguese throne in 1640.", "Her children and their descendants played crucial roles in Portuguese court politics, military endeavors, and colonial administration for centuries."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "infante-peter-duke-of-coimbra", "sourceName": "Infante Peter, Duke of Coimbra", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "infanta-philippa-of-coimbra", "targetName": "Infanta Philippa of Coimbra", "context": "Infante Peter's royal status and political ambitions directly shaped the context of Infanta Philippa's upbringing and future dynastic role."}, {"sourceSlug": "infanta-philippa-of-coimbra", "sourceName": "Infanta Philippa of Coimbra", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "alvaro-de-braganza-count-of-odemira", "targetName": "Álvaro de Braganza, Count of Odemira", "context": "Infanta Philippa collaborated with Don Álvaro de Braganza through their marriage in 1472, forming a dynastic alliance."}, {"sourceSlug": "infanta-philippa-of-coimbra", "sourceName": "Infanta Philippa of Coimbra", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "kingdom-of-portugal", "targetName": "Kingdom of Portugal", "context": "Infanta Philippa's entire life and political significance occurred within